WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.800
Part 2. You will hear the manager of a child care service at a primary school talking to

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:13.200
parents at an open day about the school's child care service offered before and after

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.000
school. First you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 15.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Good afternoon. My name's Mrs Carter and I run the before and after school extended hours child care service.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.000
I hope you've had a chance to have a good look around the school and talk to staff and pupils.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:21.000
I know that many of you are interested in using our child care service when your child joins the school

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:28.000
and perhaps you already know something about it, but for those that don't, I'll go through the main details now.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:36.000
We offer child care for children from the ages of 4 to 11, both before and after school.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.000
I know that many parents who work find this service invaluable.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:48.000
You can leave your child with us, safe in the knowledge that they will be extremely well cared for.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:57.000
We are ensured to provide care for up to 70 children, although we rarely have this many attending at any one session.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:03.000
I think we generally expect around 50 to 60 children for the afternoon sessions

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.000
and about half that number for the breakfast sessions.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Although we currently do have 70 children registered with us, not all of these attend every day.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.000
It's 10 years since we began offering an extended hours service and we've come a long way during that time.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.000
When we first opened, we only had about 20 children attending regularly.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:34.000
We try to keep our costs as low as we can and we think we provide very good value for money.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:41.000
For the afternoon sessions, which run from 3.30 until 6pm, it's £7.20,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:51.000
but if you prefer, you can pay for one hour only, which costs £3.50, or two hours, which costs £5.70.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:56.000
The cost of the childcare includes food and snacks.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:03.000
They'll be given breakfast in the morning and, in the afternoon, a healthy snack as soon as they finish school.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:10.000
At 5pm, children are given something more substantial, such as pasta or a casserole.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:19.000
Please inform us of any allergies that your child might have and we'll make sure they're offered a suitable alternative.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:26.000
As you may know, the childcare service runs through the school holidays from 8am to 6pm.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.000
We offer a really varied and exciting programme to keep the children entertained.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.000
We don't want them to feel as if they are still at school.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:42.000
It will also feel different because they'll get the chance to make new friends with children from other schools.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:49.000
Spaces are available for them because a lot of our term-time children don't always attend during the holiday.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:57.000
In the past, parents have asked if children over the age of 11 are allowed to come with their younger brothers and sisters,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:03.000
but I'm afraid we're unable to do this because of the type of insurance we have.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:43.000
Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:51.000
So now let me tell you about some of the activities that your child can do during the after-school sessions.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:57.000
As well as being able to use the playground equipment, computers and the library,

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:02.000
there is usually at least one special activity that children can do each day.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.000
For example, Spanish.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:12.000
We have a specialist teacher coming in every Thursday to give a basic introduction to the language through games and songs.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:18.000
She does two sessions, one for the over-8s and one for the younger children.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:25.000
This is the only activity which we have to make an extra charge for, but it's well worth it.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.000
Once a week, the children have the opportunity to do some music.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.000
We're very lucky that one of our staff is a member of a folk band.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:40.000
On Mondays, she teaches singing and percussion to groups of children.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:46.000
We do rely on parental support for this, so if any of you sing or play an instrument

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:51.000
and would be prepared to help out at these sessions, we'd be delighted.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:56.000
Painting continues to be one of the most popular activities.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.000
To begin with, we weren't keen on offering this because of the extra mess involved,

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:07.000
but children kept asking if they could do some art, and so we finally gave in.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:13.000
Art is great for helping the children to relax after working hard at school all day.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:17.000
Yoga is something that we've been meaning to introduce for some time,

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:23.000
but haven't been able to find anyone available to teach it, until now that is.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.000
So we'll see how this goes.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:30.000
Hopefully, children will benefit in all sorts of ways from this.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.000
Cooking is another popular activity.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:38.000
They make a different sort of cake or pizza or bread each week.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Although the younger children love doing it, we found that the mess was just too much,

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.000
so we've decided to restrict this to the over-eights,

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.000
as they are better able to clean up after themselves.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:56.000
That is the end of part two.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:00.000
You now have half a minute to check your answers to part two.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.000
.

